                  <provenance type="#b c" cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_122">Canterbury, Kent.
                        Benedictine abbey of St Augustine (originally of St Peter and St Paul)</orgName><p>Binding leaf (fol. 109) from a rent-roll, s. xiv -- place
                        names, Faversham, Tenterden, Middleton, Sheldwych, Lenham, Plomstede,
                        'sancti Pauli'.</p><p>On fol. 107v a note on the meaning of the name Mildred
                        (a Kentish saint).</p><p>On fol. 108v: 'Vsibus hoc christi templo edgyua
                        dedisti / sic augustini querens virtute tueri'. 'Superscripto pat&lt;e&gt;ne
                        pro corpore christi in cena domini'.</p><p>At top of fol. iv verso, 'ARNOLD'
                        in large leters (cf. MRJ, Ancient Libraries, pp. lxxiii,
                     538).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Liber Ioannis [Tw]y[ne] ex dono [. . . .]
                     patris sui 1578' on fol. 1r, erased but visible by u-v light. The Twynes were
                     Canterbury collectors.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Marginal notes by John Joscelyn.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">John Stow signs.</provenance>
